# scoreboard.tsv — the PERMANENT ledger for {{CAMPAIGN_TITLE}}. One row per experiment.
# RULES: tab-separated; append-only in ROWS. Never delete or rename a column mid-campaign (it breaks
#   comparability with earlier rows). Keep the PRIMARY column ({{PRIMARY_METRIC_COL}}) position stable.
#   Add campaign-specific columns AFTER the lever columns and BEFORE `verified`; a new column requires the
#   run-writer ({{EVAL_WRITER}}) to emit it. exp_id: 000 = baseline gate, 001 = first method, then 002,003,…;
#   sub-runs 000a/000b; non-config probes prefixed `#`.
# THE RUNNER WRITES EVERY CELL. The row lands when the experiment records; the NARRATIVE cells are stamped
#   in place afterwards: `what` (the config's one-line `_comment`) and `expected_vs_found` at record time;
#   `verified` from the verdict artifact (the driver); `note` (optional, at most 200 chars, for what the
#   numbers do not show) and `finding` (one line citing its verdict, when a result settles something) through
#   `python scripts/run_campaign.py --record <exp> [--ledger-note "..."] [--finding "..."]`. Never edit this
#   file by hand. The narrative of an experiment is its `results/logbook.md` entry; the campaign's working
#   memory is `results/JOURNAL.md`. This ledger is the one-line timeline the brief delivers as a projection.
# COMPARABILITY (the most common silent landmine): `metric_version` / `data_version` tag the FROZEN metric
#   and the dataset/version this row was scored under (e.g. `v1`, `v2_corrected`). A "current best" / ranking
#   claim is valid ONLY WITHIN one (metric_version, data_version) pair — NEVER compare a number across
#   versions. When the metric or data changes, bump the tag and RE-SCORE saved contenders under the new
#   version before comparing; a programmatic check should refuse a cross-version current-best (campaign-status
#   flags it). Every row MUST carry both tags — a blank tag makes the row uncomparable and is a hygiene fail.
# `tier` = the run-length tier from campaign.md §{{RUN_NOUN}} Caps (Scout / Confirmation / Extended; `Baseline` for exp 000).
#   Keep it on EVERY row so scout/confirmation cap-compliance stays machine-auditable — a real campaign lost
#   its tier tag partway through and cap-compliance became unverifiable.
exp_id	timestamp	metric_version	data_version	tier	what	{{LEVER_COLUMNS}}	{{PRIMARY_METRIC_COL}}	{{PRIMARY_SPREAD_COL}}	{{GUARDRAIL_COL}}	{{DIAGNOSTIC_COLUMNS}}	{{RUN_COLUMNS}}	expected_vs_found	verified	note	finding
